excerpts.content:
for 1:
– libp2p Gossip: the Fork Digest is part of the gossip Topic name string.
– libp2p Req/Resp: the Fork Digest context is sent as a prefix: https://github.com/ethereum/consensus-specs/blob/dev/specs/altair/p2p-interface.md#forkdigest-context
– REST SSZ: the Fork Digest is derivable from `Eth-Consensus-Version` HTTP header, in all responses. For `LightClientUpdate` array, it is interleaved with the data.
– REST JSON: the Fork Digest is derivable from various `version` properties

for 2:
– always attested header slot. this is the canonical format exchanged over the network

for 3:
– yes, it is always consistent. If your `LightClientStore` is from a later fork, you can use the `upgrade` helpers to convert older data to be processable with latest `LightClientStore`.
